{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1156659-life-magic-and-brain-damage","id":1156659,"title":"Life magic and brain damage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-07T06:49:29-08:00","id":1156659,"title":"Life magic and brain damage","content":"So what happens if you use your character with Life 3 to directly damage the brain of another character? Would be instant death if you at least score enough successes to deal damage? I mean, we are talking bout the brain... Would you have to do a long ritual (perhaps with Correspondence 3) and score at least 5 or 6 successes to achieve it? Should the ST demand to roll Medicine (perhaps even having Medicine 3 or 4) to even perform such a thing? Would it be Coincidental or Vulgar? I mean, people in stressful jobs having brain hemorrage it's not unheard of... Although I guess you should damage the brain in a way it would be believable in an autopsy to just declare it a brain hemorrafe. Also since the only witness would be the attacked person and his brain would probably not register what happened to him it is kind of difficult to count it as such...<br /> <br /> Am I overthinking this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13478-drakeepsilon","name":"DrakeEpsilon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13478_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T08:02:13-08:00","id":1156682,"title":"","content":"I think it'd be vulgar, so you'd need to score at least 4 successes on a base diff. of 7. (3+4). With that, you'd deal 8 aggravated health levels and that'd enough to kill a human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T08:37:16-08:00","id":1156695,"title":"","content":"Yeah you're over thinking it. Life 3 to deal aggravated damage. Since it heals very slowly, and only with the proper medical care, they might not survive at all if you don't finish them off instantly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T08:41:48-08:00","id":1156699,"title":"","content":"This is one of those gaming abstraction discussions. In general, nothing is going to break if you say the spell does X number of points of damage that manifest in whatever way is appropriate to the organ you targeted. So what if the spell does 3 inch lacerations if done on the quadriceps but only bursts a few small vessels if done on the brain? That just means you are accomplishing what you set out to do (making it harder to target the brain) without actually having to do any extra calculations or slow the game down.<br /> <br /> For the same reason, I would only make the player roll medicine (or other trait) if they were trying to achieve a specific effect other than/in addition to the damage.<br /> <br /> The coincidental vs vulgar of internal wounds is always tricky. In theory, people shouldn't be able to tell that you are bleeding out through a renal artery either so wouldn't that also be coincidental?. My advice is go with your gut and your game needs on this one. If you think that kind of thing would be coincidental go with that, just be willing to revisit your decision if things get out of control If you feel that it should be vulgar (or need it to be), well... there are plenty of scenarios where doing something with magic is Vulgar even though there are recorded cases of it happening in real life (see surviving a fall from a plane). Seeing someone go from healthy to dying for no discernible reason is <i>terrifying</i>. It seems unnatural even when it happens for completely normal reasons. There's every reason for a hypothetical observer to reject it when it happens.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T09:57:12-08:00","id":1156718,"title":"","content":"A targeted attack on the head or extra successes for using correspondence to deliver the spell. Damage as per spell damage chart, aggravated. If a player has life 3, I assume (or demand) decent knowledge of medicin, in one way or the other, but maybe make him/her roll int+medicine to achive the effect. Vulgar? I'd like it to be, but it isn't, as long as you keep it clean and simple. Maybe, if you just touch the target instead of giving him a solid smack on the back of his head, then it's vulgar. (Touching someone and he dies? Seems vulgar to me.)<br /> The &quot;from a distance&quot; version, using correspondence, might be more vulgar. I'm assuming this attack, with 3-4 successes does not make some blood vessels burst, but destroyes major parts of the targets brain, directly! A subtle, coincidental version would be a ritual that deals single points of damage over a few days or even weeks, slowly killing the target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T10:34:39-08:00","id":1156727,"title":"","content":"I think I'd rule it coincidental. A clot, a stroke, all terrifying things but still widely accepted by people, it's not against the consensus. I also think this kind of damage is supposed to be lethal, though- not that it makes any difference for a human, but you're not disintegrating a Vampire with this kind of attack.<br /> <br /> About damage or insta death, the only thing the system gives you is &quot;damage&quot;. You score three damage on the arm, then meat opens up, you score three damage in the brain then it's a small clot that hurt and fades away, or strong nausea and vertigo, or whatever you like. So, cutting the brain apart like you'd do with an arm is going to require more successes. Insta-kill is 7 damages, as always.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T07:22:33-08:00","id":1156992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1156659-life-magic-and-brain-damage?p=1156727#post1156727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I'd rule it coincidental. A clot, a stroke, all terrifying things but still widely accepted by people, it's not against the consensus. I also think this kind of damage is supposed to be lethal, though- not that it makes any difference for a human, but you're not disintegrating a Vampire with this kind of attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that you mention it... Can you attack a vampire brain with this kind of attack? How would that go? I guess you would need Matter for that (dead cells and all) but, how does brain damage affects a vampire? Can they resist the spell with any discipline?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13478-drakeepsilon","name":"DrakeEpsilon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13478_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T10:24:09-08:00","id":1157047,"title":"","content":"Guys, the Hypthetical Average Observer rule dictates vulgarity. If the average observer sees this happen and believes it's possible it is coincidental. If not, it's vulgar. The average observer might believe different things depending on where you're located. In modern America it's perfectly possible that people just fall over dead with no observable reasons other than expressions of pain from the individual dying. Most folks would even call for help from passerby or emergency responders. The effect is coincidental.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T10:51:50-08:00","id":1157055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrakeEpsilon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1156659-life-magic-and-brain-damage?p=1156992#post1156992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that you mention it... Can you attack a vampire brain with this kind of attack? How would that go? I guess you would need Matter for that (dead cells and all) but, how does brain damage affects a vampire? Can they resist the spell with any discipline?</div> </div> </div> </div>AFAIK, Life effects on vampires halve their successes unless you use them in conjunction with Matter. Brain damage would still be lethal, but soakable with constitution and healable as normal lethal damage. And there is no discipline or power at all able to shield a vampire from Awakened magick.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T11:15:24-08:00","id":1157061,"title":"","content":"I'm with the &quot;you're overcomplicating&quot; band.<br /> <br /> If you just want to do damage, just do damage. &quot;it's a stroke&quot; is all you need to declare, presuming your Practices allow it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T12:37:41-08:00","id":1157612,"title":"","content":"If you want some specific type of brain damage, then I'd rule your character needs an ability which tells them where to target the attack. Life 3 is sufficient for the magick and you can directly target a pattern, so you don't need Correspondence if your target is within unaided visual range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T19:13:35-08:00","id":1157675,"title":"","content":"Little clarification on a thing I wrote: both life AND matter do half damage against vampires. For a full damage efffect you need to use them in conjunction (or set for a different Sphere).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T19:41:06-08:00","id":1157679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1156659-life-magic-and-brain-damage?p=1157675#post1157675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Little clarification on a thing I wrote: both life AND matter do half damage against vampires. For a full damage efffect you need to use them in conjunction (or set for a different Sphere).</div> </div> </div> </div>What? Could I get a reference? I missed that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T01:27:50-08:00","id":1157716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1156659-life-magic-and-brain-damage?p=1157679#post1157679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What? Could I get a reference? I missed that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Under M20, it's even *required* to use both in conjunction to affect a Vampire with effects emulating Life. Though you need Life 3 but only Matter 2. See Page 508 in M20 core and a quip on Page 517, and for Revised see Page 280.<br /> Interestingly that Revised page also states that you *require* to use both Spheres.<br /> I can't find the 'half damage' rule for using *only* Life Or Matter in Revised core right now, but I do remember that rule.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> Found it, Mage Storytellers Handbook (revised) Page 201, gives optional rules, like allowing half damage through only using Life or Matter.<br /> <br /> But the default, in Both Revised AND M20, is literally having to use Life 3 + Matter 2 for any Life-3-like effects on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T02:17:21-08:00","id":1157720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1156659-life-magic-and-brain-damage?p=1157716#post1157716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the default, in Both Revised AND M20, is literally having to use Life 3 + Matter 2 for any Life-3-like effects on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, I somehow remembered this to be the the optional rule. =p<br /> And yes, Life needs to be higher because Life 2 only allows you to rewrite your own pattern and you'll need 3 to affect others.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T09:45:38-08:00","id":1157773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1156659-life-magic-and-brain-damage?p=1157716#post1157716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Under M20, it's even *required* to use both in conjunction to affect a Vampire with effects emulating Life. Though you need Life 3 but only Matter 2. See Page 508 in M20 core and a quip on Page 517, and for Revised see Page 280.<br /> Interestingly that Revised page also states that you *require* to use both Spheres.<br /> I can't find the 'half damage' rule for using *only* Life Or Matter in Revised core right now, but I do remember that rule.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> Found it, Mage Storytellers Handbook (revised) Page 201, gives optional rules, like allowing half damage through only using Life or Matter.<br /> <br /> But the default, in Both Revised AND M20, is literally having to use Life 3 + Matter 2 for any Life-3-like effects on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems, odd. Vampires are dead thing, which falls under the life sphere(you only need life 5 to restore life to something, it'll still be soulless and have no mind though). So why are vamps different,it doesn't prevent &quot;Lawn Chair&quot; as you need matter for that anyway and it doesn't prevent a correspondence/forces magic from ritual blasting one from across a continent. Is it to prevent a life mage from bring every vampire he walks across back to life? I imagine you'd need prime 5 in edition to life 5 to clean the vampire's nasty resonance-laden quint anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T11:01:14-08:00","id":1157788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1156659-life-magic-and-brain-damage?p=1157773#post1157773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That seems, odd. Vampires are dead thing, which falls under the life sphere(you only need life 5 to restore life to something, it'll still be soulless and have no mind though). So why are vamps different,it doesn't prevent &quot;Lawn Chair&quot; as you need matter for that anyway and it doesn't prevent a correspondence/forces magic from ritual blasting one from across a continent. Is it to prevent a life mage from bring every vampire he walks across back to life? I imagine you'd need prime 5 in edition to life 5 to clean the vampire's nasty resonance-laden quint anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on the state of decay you also need Matter to revive a corpse, along with Mind and Spirit to restore the soul and a sound Mind. It's never simply Life 5.<br /> <br /> Vampires are trapped in a perpetual state of undeath. Neither living or dead. That's why it takes Matter and Life to effect their Pattern directly. Just like how Werewolves are half spirit, and need Spirit 2 to effect their Pattern directly. Supernatural monsters are more complex than normal living things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T11:13:45-08:00","id":1157792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PazuzuAxelf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1156659-life-magic-and-brain-damage?p=1157788#post1157788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depending on the state of decay you also need Matter to revive a corpse, along with Mind and Spirit to restore the soul and a sound Mind. It's never simply Life 5.<br /> <br /> Vampires are trapped in a perpetual state of undeath. Neither living or dead. That's why it takes Matter and Life to effect their Pattern directly. Just like how Werewolves are half spirit, and need Spirit 2 to effect their Pattern directly. Supernatural monsters are more complex than normal living things.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd only need matter on a decayed corpse to replace lost flesh and there's no state of decay on a vamp. So I really don't buy that explanation.<br /> <br /> It reads to me like needing forces as well as matter to build a phone and explaining it as because the phone needs electricity to work. All I can think is why can't you just build the phone with matter and install a mundane battery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T11:23:44-08:00","id":1157794,"title":"","content":"M20 pg. 508 - under the Body Works chart <br /> <br /> Heal/ Harm Fae - Life 3/ Mind 3<br /> Heal/ Harm Vampire - Life 3/ Matter 2<br /> Heal/ Harm Werecreature - Life 3/ Spirit 2<br /> <br /> M20 pg. 516 - under the entry for Life<br /> <br /> As a whole, this Sphere embraces everything that has living cells within itself, even if that object is technically dead. As a general rule, assume that anything that\u2019s still alive enough to transplant, preserve, or cultivate is governed by Life Arts. If it\u2019s inert enough to be irrevocably dead, then it\u2019s governed by Matter. Thus, preserved blood and organs, still-living plants, live-culture cheese, and so forth contain Life, but corpses, cotton fibers, withered organs, or cut wood become Matter. <br /> <br /> M20 pg. 517 - under the entry for Matter<br /> <br /> Life plus Matter bridges the gap between living and dead materials \u2013 an essential combination when dealing with vampires \u2013 and Spirit plus Matter renders ephemera into matter or matter into ephemera. <br /> <br /> <br /> Like it or not, that's how it works. House rule it for your own game if you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T17:24:04-08:00","id":1157838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1156659-life-magic-and-brain-damage?p=1157773#post1157773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That seems, odd. Vampires are dead thing, which falls under the life sphere(you only need life 5 to restore life to something, it'll still be soulless and have no mind though). So why are vamps different,</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no.<br /> Remember that the Life sphere encompasses two distinct but intermingable and confusable things: Biological life as we understand it, and metaphysical life-force, for a lack of a better term. And vampires essentially still have lifeforce, trapped inside a static, entropy-less dead body.<br /> They are in a weird Schroedinger's Cat state between alive and dead, not completely inert on all fronts, but not dynamic either. But since that trapped lifeforce and the dead body are intertwined, you require both spheres to affect it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T12:08:07-08:00","id":1157974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1156659-life-magic-and-brain-damage?p=1157792#post1157792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'd only need matter on a decayed corpse to replace lost flesh and there's no state of decay on a vamp. So I really don't buy that explanation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only Matter won't work because they're not just dead: the brain is still alive-ish, proved by how attacks to their head do lethal damage, and the body is often storing more life force than a regular human (= more than 10 blood points), even if static. Only Life won't work because they're not quite alive: no reproduction, no bodily functions, no possible growth, they don't fit any definition of &quot;life&quot;.<br /> <br /> About &quot;just Life 5 to resurrect&quot;, I happen to own a 3rd edition supplement called &quot;The Red Sign&quot;, a crossover campaign where a group of Awakened and blood mages tries to return a vampire to life. One of the three required rituals for the task (and the reason for me to bring this out) is the Invocation of Eternity, that on its own allows a Mage to return a recently dead to life.<br /> <br /> The Rote is stated difficulty 11 (impossible without the tome describing it) and requiring Life 5, Matter 2, Prime 2, Spirit 2 and Time 2: without Time you can only cast it on someone the moment the man died, and without Spirit you can't meld the soul to the body, leaving it an empty husk open to supernatural possession. Without Matter and Prime, though, you just can't raise the dead.<br /> <br /> Spirit is only 2 because the ritual is for the recently dead, grabbing the soul before it moves on in the reincarnation cycle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13673,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","user":"Maris Streck","date":". 11-12-2017, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T13:46:44-08:00","id":1157986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1156659-life-magic-and-brain-damage?p=1157974#post1157974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Only Matter won't work because they're not just dead: the brain is still alive-ish, proved by how attacks to their head do lethal damage, and the body is often storing more life force than a regular human (= more than 10 blood points), even if static. Only Life won't work because they're not quite alive: no reproduction, no bodily functions, no possible growth, they don't fit any definition of &quot;life&quot;.<br /> <br /> About &quot;just Life 5 to resurrect&quot;, I happen to own a 3rd edition supplement called &quot;The Red Sign&quot;, a crossover campaign where a group of Awakened and blood mages tries to return a vampire to life. One of the three required rituals for the task (and the reason for me to bring this out) is the Invocation of Eternity, that on its own allows a Mage to return a recently dead to life.<br /> <br /> The Rote is stated difficulty 11 (impossible without the tome describing it) and requiring Life 5, Matter 2, Prime 2, Spirit 2 and Time 2: without Time you can only cast it on someone the moment the man died, and without Spirit you can't meld the soul to the body, leaving it an empty husk open to supernatural possession. Without Matter and Prime, though, you just can't raise the dead.<br /> <br /> Spirit is only 2 because the ritual is for the recently dead, grabbing the soul before it moves on in the reincarnation cycle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, what? My arguement was for vampires falling under the life sphere as dead creatures.<br /> <br /> Wasn't there a version of that rote in revised specifically for reviving the dead-non-vamps(I don't remember if it was core, guide to the traditions, book of madness or I'm just forgeting the book title) the time component on that rote was so that you could find the spirit via the moment it died(as in you didn't need it if the soul was present).<br /> <br /> I can now say I'm entirely confused on the is a dead thing life or matter as the life sphere itself describes dead/formerly-alive things as falling under life, but all rotes involving dead things use matter as well. It might have been edited in post and I just have an old PDF.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T22:28:12-08:00","id":1158085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1156659-life-magic-and-brain-damage?p=1157986#post1157986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um, what? My arguement was for vampires falling under the life sphere as dead creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just saying that RAW not only vampires but even dead humans require Matter conjunction to apply a Life effect. I did not find a raise dead rote on 3rd edition core, but even there Life is described as changing a living pattern; and afaik, rule-wise killing someone is the classic method to switch from Life to Matter.<br /> <br /> M20 says:<br /> <br /> <i>As a whole, this Sphere embraces everything that has living cells within itself, even if that object is technically dead. As a general rule, assume that anything that\u2019s still alive enough to transplant, preserve, or cultivate is governed by Life Arts. If it\u2019s inert enough to be irrevocably dead, then it\u2019s governed by Matter. Thus, preserved blood and organs, still-living plants, live-culture cheese, and so forth contain Life, but corpses, cotton fibers, withered organs, or cut wood become Matter.</i><br /> <br /> I'm also reading that, actually, under M20 rules Life magic does aggravate damage because it rewrites the victim's pattern (p. 516 M20).<br /> M20 doesn't seem to consider limitations to multiple Life effects on the same target, while Revised actually specified that you can't alter the same pattern twice in the same scene (because your Arete roll considers all the possible changes to that pattern for the time).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13673,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","user":"Maris Streck","date":". 11-13-2017, 01:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T08:11:05-08:00","id":1158170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1156659-life-magic-and-brain-damage?p=1158085#post1158085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just saying that RAW not only vampires but even dead humans require Matter conjunction to apply a Life effect. I did not find a raise dead rote on 3rd edition core, but even there Life is described as changing a living pattern; and afaik, rule-wise killing someone is the classic method to switch from Life to Matter.<br /> <br /> M20 says:<br /> <br /> <i>As a whole, this Sphere embraces everything that has living cells within itself, even if that object is technically dead. As a general rule, assume that anything that\u2019s still alive enough to transplant, preserve, or cultivate is governed by Life Arts. If it\u2019s inert enough to be irrevocably dead, then it\u2019s governed by Matter. Thus, preserved blood and organs, still-living plants, live-culture cheese, and so forth contain Life, but corpses, cotton fibers, withered organs, or cut wood become Matter.</i><br /> <br /> I'm also reading that, actually, under M20 rules Life magic does aggravate damage because it rewrites the victim's pattern (p. 516 M20).<br /> M20 doesn't seem to consider limitations to multiple Life effects on the same target, while Revised actually specified that you can't alter the same pattern twice in the same scene (because your Arete roll considers all the possible changes to that pattern for the time).</div> </div> </div> </div>Welp, I was wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T14:09:44-08:00","id":1158630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrakeEpsilon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1156659-life-magic-and-brain-damage?p=1156992#post1156992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that you mention it... Can you attack a vampire brain with this kind of attack? How would that go? I guess you would need Matter for that (dead cells and all) but, how does brain damage affects a vampire? Can they resist the spell with any discipline?</div> </div> </div> </div>I also need to correct myself.<br /> The Mage Storyteller Handbook (3rd ed supplement) suggests that Thaumaturgists could be able to counter Awakened magic by &quot;rolling Thaumaturgy&quot; (I think they mean the discipline, not the Willpower roll) with the Mage's willpower as difficulty and counter 1 success on the Arete roll every 2 successes. Owning Thaumaturgical countermagic adds 1 success for each dot of Countermagic owned.<br /> <br /> The Handbook also states that you can't counter an effect you don't know it's coming, so you can unweave an incoming fireball but surely not counter an aneurysm.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Re-correcting myself. M20 says that Vulgar life effects inflicts aggravated damages while coincidental ones only lethal. So, Conjure Aneurysm would be only lethal, unless powered with Prime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13673,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","user":"Maris Streck","date":". 12-04-2017, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}